# React Doctor Timing

Follow `.cursor/rules/selective-verification.mdc`. There is no UI-file-count or commit/push threshold. Run React Doctor when requested or when its diagnostics can resolve a material React correctness, accessibility, or integration concern.

Use the shared `react-doctor` skill for the current CLI workflow. Once relevant diagnostics are handled, repeat the affected scan only if changes or unresolved concerns justify it; do not loop for a higher score.
